QuestGuidance.Register("en",371,{
[11841]="70057813\n1\tFind Lumrog\tDeep within Lumrog, a fearsome hill-troll keeps the other creatures there in line. This beast is Torask-rúm, the Butcher of Lumrog, and if he is defeated the resolve of his underlings may waver.\n2\tDefeat Torask-rúm, the Butcher of Lumrog\tTorask-rúm, the Butcher of Lumrog, is a fearsome hill-troll keeps the other creatures within Lumrog in line. Defeating this creature should break the resolve of his underlings.\n3\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[11842]="7002FE09\n1\tFollow Fastred's trail outside of Snowbourn\tGísling recommends setting out to the east of Snowbourn in search of Fastred or any Orcs that he has slain in his wake. Gísling suggests that you try to find Fastred in the field and persuade him to return to Snowbourn.\n2\tFollow Fastred's trail of slaughtered Orcs\tGísling recommends setting out to the east of Snowbourn in search of Fastred or any Orcs that he has slain in his wake. Gísling suggests that you try to find Fastred in the field and persuade him to return to Snowbourn.\n3\tFollow Fastred's trail of slaughtered Orcs\tGísling recommends setting out to the east of Snowbourn in search of Fastred or any Orcs that he has slain in his wake. Gísling suggests that you try to find Fastred in the field and persuade him to return to Snowbourn.\n4\tFollow Fastred's trail of slaughtered Orcs\tGísling recommends setting out to the east of Snowbourn in search of Fastred or any Orcs that he has slain in his wake. Gísling suggests that you try to find Fastred in the field and persuade him to return to Snowbourn.\n5\tFind Fastred\tYou have followed Fastred's trail of slaughter far into the Sutcrofts. He must be nearby. You should search for Fastred.\n6\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found near Dagred's grave to the west and slightly north of Snowbourn. You should deliver Gísling's message to Fastred.\n",
[11843]="70020C34\n1\tThere may be dead oxen among the herds of the Uch-lûth at Uch Cadlus in the Windfells. Alun has asked you to examine the dead oxen among the herds of the Uch-lûth to determine what may have slain them.\t\n2\tDefeat the Black Sow of the Windfells\tThe Black Sow wanders the wilds of the Windfells. Having determined that a great boar did indeed slay the oxen of the Uch-lûth, you should hunt down the Black Sow of the Windfells.\n3\tTalk to Alun at Uch Cadlus\tAlun is at Uch Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith. You should return to Alun with news of your success.\n",
[11844]="70002D14\n1\tObtain a stone from the Cairn of Honour\tThe Cairn of Honour is in the centre of Fasach-Falroid to the north of Aughaire. It is atop a high hill, west of the north road, and at night the path to it is lit by torches. Arzhur has asked you to obtain a stone from the Cairn of Honour. You must not spill any blood of the Hillmen who patrol the area.\n2\tBring the Cairn-stone to Arzhur\tArzhur is back at Aughaire. You should bring the stone you recovered to Arzhur and prepare for the next challenge.\n",
[11845]="70054897\n1\tTalk to Halhir\tHalhir can be found somewhere along the Morgul-road, somewhere to the west. You should find Halhir.\n",
[11846]="7002272B\n1\tTake rubbings of the ancient pillars (total: 3)\tThe ruins on the southern hills lie to the south of Nár's Peak, through the mountain pass. Frithgeir has asked you to seek out the ruined pillars among the ancient dwarf-ruins and take rubbings of the runes found upon them.\n2\tTalk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund within Nár's Peak, north of the ruins, through the mountain pass. You should return to Frithgeir and present him with the rubbings of these pillars.\n",
[11847]="7006906F\n1\tInvestigate the island\tThere are reports of sailors disappearing in the northern Shield Isles. Investigate the islands and figure out what is happening to these sailors.\n2\tDefeat siren slayers (total: 7)\030Defeat siren stalkers (total: 5)\tEscape the island!\n3\tDefeat Sadâjah the Cruel\t\n",
[11848]="700428C4\n1\tThe market of Michel Delving is south of Bingo's hobbit-hole. Bingo Boffin has decided to throw a dinner-party for his neighbours in order to relieve some of his loneliness, and wants you to assess the available food at the market. He hopes it will inspire him on the matter of what courses to serve at his party.\t\n2\tReturn to Bingo and give him your report\tBingo Boffin is outside his hobbit-hole north of the Michel Delving market, on the other side of the Town Hole. You have assessed a number of foods at the market in Michel Delving, and should now report back to Bingo Boffin.\n3\tTravel to the library in the Great Smials, in Tuckborough, and speak to the librarian there\tThe library in the Great Smials is in the town of Tuckborough, east of Michel Delving. Uninspired by your report of the delicious food for sale at the market, Bingo thinks that perhaps a cookbook will give him the inspiration he needs.\n4\tCheck out one of the fine cookbooks behind Donnamira Took\tDonnamira Took, the librarian in the Great Smials, has recommended a cookbook from the shelf behind her.\n5\tBring the fine cookbook to Bingo outside his hobbit-hole\tBingo is outside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, just north of the the Town Hole. You have checked out a fine cookbook from the library in the Great Smials and should bring it to Bingo.\n6\tBring the map to Keeper Brombard Foxtail at the Mathom-house\tThe Mathom-house of Michel Delving is on a hill south-west of Bingo Boffin's hobbit-hole. Bingo has asked you to bring the map that fell out of the library's cookbook to the Mathom-house in Michel Delving. He does not want it.\n7\tTalk to Bingo on the road that climbs the hill to the Mathom-house\tBingo has run up the hill to the Mathom-house at break-neck speed, and is now exhausted. What could he want?\n8\tTalk to Bingo Boffin outside his hobbit-hole\tBingo has asked to meet you once again outside his hobbit-hole to the north-east of the Mathom-house, north of the Town Hole. Bingo has been inspired by the hand-drawn map he found, but not to host a dinner-party. Instead, he wants to go on an adventure!\n",
[11849]="7005AABE\n1\tFind Klúso\tKlúso is east of Out-camp Stazg Vozag, spying on the hobgoblins. You should find Klúso and help him however you can.\n2\tComplete 'Sentries from the Out-camp'\030Complete 'Swords in the Shadows'\030Complete 'Storming Stazg Vozag'\030Complete 'Enemy Intelligence'\030Find information about Loknashra\tKlúso needs your help.\n3\tTalk to Klúso\tKlúso is east of Out-camp Stazg Vozag, spying on the hobgoblins.\n",
[11850]="70046C54\n1\tVisit the Cathlond, the cape docks\030Visit the Court of Anglind\030Visit the interior of Narvindon\030Take a boat to one of the islands off the coast\030Visit one of the smaller houses on the Cape\030Visit one of the standard sized houses on the Cape\030Visit one of the largest houses on the Cape\tFalastír wants you to see the sites of the Cape of Belfalas.\n2\tTalk to Falastír\tFalastír is located at the lighthouse on the Cape of Belfalas. You should let Falastír know that you have toured the Cape as he suggested.\n",
[11851]="70040B00\n1\tFind and confront Tabadam at Makham Mijann\tTabadam can be found at the corsair camp Makham Mijann. Find and confront Tabadam at Makham Mijann.\n2\tSpeak with Bruidis in the village of Tadrent\tBruidis can be found in the village of Tadrent. You should report back to Bruidis and inform her of Tabadam's defeat.\n",
[11852]="70015E41\n1\tThe battle-horn is in the camp east of the pond at Sâd Rechu, east of Gwingris. Inufileg has instructed you to use the Dunlendings' battle-horn to issue a challenge to their leader, Tudur.\t\n2\tTalk to Inufileg at Gwingris\tInufileg is at Gwingris, west of Sâd Rechu. You should return to Gwingris and tell Inufileg of your success.\n",
[11853]="7003A473\n1\tDefeat captains of Madh-fushaum (0/3)\tThere are captains among the White Hand army inside Madh-fushaum. You should defeat the White Hand captains, for their defeat would surely cause turmoil among the ranks present.\n2\tThere are captains among the White Hand army inside Madh-fushaum. You should defeat the White Hand captains, for their defeat would surely cause turmoil among the ranks present.\t\n3\tComplete\tYou have succeeded in defeating the captains within Madh-fushaum, and already you can hear sounds of confusion coming from the distance.\n",
[11854]="7004B2E0\n1\tDefeat Captain Shárdul\030Defeat Mordor Captains (total: 5)\tShárdul and his captains can be found at the Mornaur Look-out. You should defeat Shárdul and Mordor Captains.\n",
[11855]="700317E2\n1\tTalk to Gísil\tGísil can be found inside the Mead Hall of Garsfeld. Gísil has ordered you and Gísling to escort the people of Garsfeld to safety in the south. He is waiting for you to make any final preparations.\n2\tTalk to Gísling\tGísling can be found in northern Snowbourn. You have successfully brought the crofters of Garsfeld to safety inside the walls of Snowbourn and should now speak to Gísling.\n",
[11856]="7004A385\n1\tShoo away goats\tGoats can be found in Udûn. You should shoo away goats.\n2\tShoo away goats (total: 8)\tGoats can be found in Udûn. You should shoo away goats.\n3\tDefeat the Caretaker\tThe Caretaker is located somewhere in near the Foundry Deck in Udûn. Defeat the Caretaker.\n4\tDefeat the Caretaker\tThe Caretaker is located somewhere near the Foundry Deck in Udûn. Defeat the Caretaker.\n5\tDefeat the Caretaker\tThe Caretaker is located somewhere near the Foundry Deck in Udûn. Defeat the Caretaker.\n6\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[11857]="70007FF3\n1\tSearch the abandoned bear den\tThe abandoned den should be north of the hunter's lodge near the standing stones. Thrasi hurt his leg while rescuing an injured lynx from hendrevail and asked you to retrieve the surviving cubs.\n2\tDefeat hendrevail (total: 6)\tThere are hendrevail throughout the woods. A frightened lynx-cub cowers in an old den, too scared to venture out into the light. You must defeat the hendrevail lurking nearby to prove that you mean it no harm.\n3\tCoax the lynx-cub from its den\tCoax the lynx-cub from its den. With the hendrevail defeated, the lynx-cub seems to feel safe enough to leave its den.\n4\tBring the lynx-cub to Thrasi\tThrasi is back at the hunter's lodge, south of here. You recovered the lynx-cub as Thrasi requested. Return it to him at the hunter's lodge.\n",
[11858]="7000135A\n1\tFind the Cauldron of Death\030Defeat the Cauldron's guardian\tThe Cauldron of Death and its guardian are before the central lake of Imlad Balchorth, west from Myrkworth. Oflár has asked you to fight your way to the Cauldron of Death and destroy its guardian. He suggested you gather allies.\n2\tTalk to Oflár\tOflár is at Myrkworth, east from the Cauldron of Death. With the Iron-bound giant destroyed, the Cauldron of Death ceased spewing forth wights, at least for now. You should return and report your success to Oflár.\n",
[11859]="7006698E\n1\tRetrieve the key to Igerna's cage\tIgerna has asked you to find the key to her cage. She suggests the overseers may be the ones to carry the keys. Goblin overseers can be found throughout the cave and in Krauzhaf, in Pinnath Gelin.\n2\tUnlock Igerna's cage\tAfter battling through the halls of Krauzhaf, you recovered an iron key that looks like it will fit the lock on Igerna's cage door. You should unlock Igerna's cage, in the cave at Krauzhaf, in Pinnath Gelin.\n3\tTalk to Igerna\tYou have unlocked Igerna's cave, and she is now waiting to speak with you. Igerna is in a cave in Krauzhaf, in northern Pinnath Gelin.\n",
[11860]="70053048\n1\tEnter Kidzul-kâlah\tShadow runes and torches can be found within Kidzul-kâlah's depths. You should destroy the shadow runes and torches that you find.\n2\tDestroy the shadow runes in Kidzul-kâlah's depths (total: 12)\030Destroy the shadow torches in Kidzul-kâlah's depths (total: 8)\tShadow runes and torches can be found within Kidzul-kâlah's depths. You should destroy the shadow runes and torches that you find.\n3\tCompleted\tDestroyed many shadow runes in Kidzul-kâlah's depths.\n",
[11861]="700001F8\n1\tUse Gates of Minas Agar\030Collect Translated Incantation\tMinas Agar stands on the western side of Barad Gularan, south of Gath Forthnír. You must travel to Barad Gularan and issue a challenge to the Angmarim within Minas Agar.\n2\tReport back to Lindir\tLindir is in the Fire Hall in Rivendell in the Trollshaws, far to the south. You travelled to the Minas Agar and called out its champion. After a difficult battle, you defeated her. You should bring news of your victory to Lindir.\n",
[11862]="700001FA\n1\tDefeat Laugi Goldentongue\030Use Gates of Minas Angos\030Collect Translated Incantation\tMinas Angos stands on the western side of Barad Gularan, south of Gath Forthnír. You must travel to Barad Gularan and issue a challenge to the evil dwarves within Minas Angos.\n2\tReport back to Lindir\tLindir is in the Fire Hall in Rivendell in the Trollshaws, far to the south. You travelled to Minas Angos and called out its dwarven champion. After a difficult battle, you defeated him. You should return to Lindir with the news of your victory\n",
[11863]="700001F7\n1\tUse Gates of Minas Caul\030Collect Translated Incantation\tMinas Caul stands on the western side of Barad Gularan, south of Gath Forthnír. You must travel to Barad Gularan and issue a challenge to the Orcs within Minas Caul.\n2\tReport back to Lindir\tLindir is in the Fire Hall in Rivendell in the Trollshaws, far to the south. You travelled to the Minas Caul and called out its champion. After a difficult battle, you defeated him. You should return to Lindir with news of your victory.\n",
[11864]="700001F9\n1\tDefeat Prakhum\030Use Gates of Minas Maur\030Collect Translated Incantation\tMinas Maur stands on the western side of Barad Gularan, south of Gath Forthnír. You must travel to Barad Gularan and issue a challenge to the goblins within Minas Maur.\n2\tReport back to Lindir\tLindir is in the Fire Hall in Rivendell in the Trollshaws, far to the south. You travelled to Minas Maur and called out its champion. After a difficult battle, you defeated the creature. You should return to Lindir with the news of your victory.\n",
[11865]="7005A693\n1\tDefeat the goblin courier\030Defeat goblin-courier defender\030Recover the champion missive\tThe goblin courier can be found on Gabilthurkhu, the Great-way, between Dursh Hûl and Kamaz-kala. Valdi has asked you to retrieve a missive from the goblin courier.\n2\tReturn to Valdi\tValdi can be found in Amdân. You should talk to Valdi.\n",
[11866]="70069827\n1\tTalk to Hadorion outside the Stonecliff Market\tKhâshap plans to confront the rumours head on by appearing before the Gut. Hadorion believes we should spring the trap now. Meet Hadorion outside the Stonecliff Market in the Gut.\n2\tCrash Khâshap's Assembly\tKhâshap has gathered his cohorts to clear his name. He must be stopped here and now.\n3\tTalk to Hadorion at the Stonecliff Market entrance\tKhâshap has fled into the alleys of the Gut under the protection of his Jephai Corsairs. Find Hadorion at the entrance of the Stonecliff Market to discuss our next move.\n",
[11867]="7001909E\n1\tCollect chickens before they escape (total: 2)\tEvery hour, chickens are released into the hedge maze in Bree. They are only there for fifteen minutes out of every hour, so catch them while you can! You must collect chickens during the time that they are running amok in the hedge maze.\n2\tTalk to Buttercup North-took outside the maze in the Horse-fields\tButtercup North-took is standing outside the maze entrance in the Horse-fields. You should speak with Buttercup North-took and tell her about all the wonderful things you accomplished inside the maze.\n",
[11868]="7004A8D7\n1\tTalk to Legolas in the Silent Haunt\tLegolas is standing in the Silent Haunt. You have tracked the Silent One to his lair in Lhingris and discovered a tattered black cloak and Orkish armour bearing a single strand of Frodo's hair. You should talk to Legolas and think of how Frodo and Sam came to disguise themselves as Orcs of Mordor.\n2\tTalk to Legolas in the Silent Haunt\tLegolas is standing in the Silent Haunt. You have thought long on the choices of Master Samwise, and should now speak to Legolas.\n",
[11869]="7000E99A\n1\tCollect the Silvan thirty-point's flank\tThe great elk can be found to the south-west of Kauppa-kohta. Cenlieg has asked you to kill the great elk and bring its flank to him.\n2\tBring the Silvan thirty-point's flank to Cenlieg\030Collect the Silvan thirty-point's flank\tCenlieg is at Kauppa-kohta, east from where you found the elk-buck. You should return to Cenlieg with the elk-flank you collected.\n",
[11870]="70055070\n1\tComplete quests in the Circle of Death (total: 10)\030Aid Prince Faramir in 'A Waxing Moon'\tYou should complete quests in the Circle of Death and aid Faramir in his plans.\n2\tTalk to Candúr in Barad Arthir\tCandúr can be found in Barad Arthir. You have aided Prince Faramir and secured the Circle of Death in Minas Morgul.\n",
[11871]="70055071\n1\tTalk to Dornach in the Circle of Despair\tDornach can be found in the Circle of Despair outside Barad Arthir. Candúr has asked for your aid in securing the Circle of Despair and has sent you to join Dornach's company. You should talk to Dornach.\n2\tAid Dornach in securing the Circle of Despair\tYou should aid Dornach in securing the Circle of Despair.\n3\tTalk to Candúr in Barad Arthir\tCandúr can be found in Barad Arthir in Minas Morgul. You should talk to Candúr.\n",
[11872]="700544B2\n1\tComplete quests in the Circle of Madness (total: 10)\tYou should complete quests in the Circle of Madness in Minas Morgul.\n2\tTalk to Rhadrog in Barad Elenath\tRhadrog can be found in Barad Elenath in Minas Morgul. You should talk to Rhadrog.\n3\tComplete 'Instance: Into the Circle of Despair'\030Enter Barad Arthir, the Lofty Watch-fort\tThe entrance to Barad Arthir can be found in the Circle of Despair. You should enter the tower of Barad Arthir.\n4\tTalk to Candúr in Barad Arthir\tCandúr can be found in Barad Arthir in Minas Morgul. You should talk to Candúr.\n",
})
